without stopping until you #offer.

> This, in case you couldn't figure that out, was super bad.  I was not
> going to survive the Planes without magic resistance of ###.

Magic resistance isn't ###, magic cancellation is.  They're different.
Magic resistance is binary, but without it you'd be in pretty big
trouble (e.g. Rodney could use the touch of death and kill you in 1
turn).

> While kicking morosely through the soldier skulls, blood-spattered
> daggers, and huge piles of C-rations at Ludios, I happened upon a
> dwarvish mithril coat.  Dwarvish mithril coat?

That has magic cancellation of ###, but only if you don't cover it with
a cloak/robe.

Luckily for you, a robe has magic cancellation of ### and the Eyes of
the Overworld grant you magic resistance.

